1
00:00:08,620 --> 00:00:11,140
Brighten up the room and try stepping back,
will you?

2
00:00:20,280 --> 00:00:24,300
Anyone without money, come to me!

3
00:00:24,300 --> 00:00:29,000
I'm broke too, but don't you worry.

4
00:00:29,000 --> 00:00:32,820
Look at that blue sky!

5
00:00:33,860 --> 00:00:36,260
White clouds.

6
00:00:36,260 --> 00:00:42,700
Things will work out somehow,
sooner or later.

7
00:00:44,700 --> 00:00:46,000
You understand, right?

8
00:00:46,000 --> 00:00:48,020
I get it, I get it.

9
00:00:48,020 --> 00:00:51,940
Once you get it, shut up and follow me.

10
00:01:05,260 --> 00:01:07,220
Jump out, Christmas!

11
00:01:18,580 --> 00:01:19,460
Done.

12
00:01:19,460 --> 00:01:20,820
Let's see.

13
00:01:21,940 --> 00:01:22,960
You're pretty good at this.

14
00:01:23,500 --> 00:01:25,940
Ryo-chan, you really do have nimble fingers.

15
00:01:26,520 --> 00:01:28,900
That's all the orders finished.

16
00:01:29,460 --> 00:01:31,620
Side jobs are truly a veteran's specialty.

17
00:01:31,620 --> 00:01:35,000
But I've got a lot more to earn if
I want to make it through the year.

18
00:01:35,000 --> 00:01:36,980
I'd better find my next part-time job.

19
00:01:37,520 --> 00:01:39,420
Ryo-san, you use people up

20
00:01:39,420 --> 00:01:42,680
and only go along with things
when it's down to the wire.

21
00:01:42,680 --> 00:01:43,340
Leave me alone.

22
00:01:43,980 --> 00:01:44,380
I know.

23
00:01:45,040 --> 00:01:45,940
Hey, Ryo-chan.

24
00:01:45,940 --> 00:01:48,640
We're short-staffed and looking for people.

25
00:01:48,640 --> 00:01:52,400
I think there's a part-time job that
would make good use of your dexterity.

26
00:01:52,400 --> 00:01:55,640
Really? I'm not picky, just hook me up.

27
00:01:55,640 --> 00:01:59,180
Sure. In return,
there's something I need your help with.

28
00:02:00,420 --> 00:02:01,220
Morning.

29
00:02:01,220 --> 00:02:02,380
Chief.

30
00:02:02,380 --> 00:02:03,780
Good morning.

31
00:02:06,000 --> 00:02:08,080
I'm not doing side jobs during work hours.

32
00:02:08,560 --> 00:02:09,620
Side jobs?

33
00:02:09,840 --> 00:02:13,040
No, no, it's nothing. It's my own business.

34
00:02:14,280 --> 00:02:17,620
Anyway, you haven't forgotten what
I asked you the other day, have you?

35
00:02:18,960 --> 00:02:19,900
What was it again?

36
00:02:19,900 --> 00:02:22,500
What's with that face? Did you forget?

37
00:02:22,500 --> 00:02:23,800
Well

38
00:02:23,800 --> 00:02:28,540
Ryo-san, the handmade sailing ship
model for the chief's grandson.

39
00:02:28,540 --> 00:02:29,960
R-right.

40
00:02:29,960 --> 00:02:33,960
Of course I haven't forgotten.
Leave it to me.

41
00:02:33,960 --> 00:02:38,080
Daisuke loves ships.
He's really looking forward to it.

42
00:02:38,080 --> 00:02:40,540
Make sure you keep your promise this time.

43
00:02:40,540 --> 00:02:43,500
I understand. Trust me.

44
00:02:47,120 --> 00:02:48,840
This is Ryotsu, our part-timer.

45
00:02:48,840 --> 00:02:51,840
From today, we have one week
until the big Christmas Eve rush.

46
00:02:51,840 --> 00:02:54,020
He'll become a full-fledged cake maker.

47
00:02:54,020 --> 00:02:55,720
Everyone, train him thoroughly.

48
00:02:55,720 --> 00:02:59,140
Can someone really become
a full-fledged pro in a week?

49
00:02:59,880 --> 00:03:00,860
Ryotsu-kun.

50
00:03:02,360 --> 00:03:03,080
Nice to meet you. I'll be in your care.

51
00:03:04,740 --> 00:03:07,540
First up is the basic of cake making:
meringue.

52
00:03:07,540 --> 00:03:09,380
So I just whisk this, right?

53
00:03:09,380 --> 00:03:10,860
Easy, easy.

54
00:03:13,120 --> 00:03:15,000
No, no, faster!

55
00:03:15,000 --> 00:03:15,940
Like this?

56
00:03:17,080 --> 00:03:18,280
Still way too slow.

57
00:03:18,280 --> 00:03:19,180
Shit!

58
00:03:19,940 --> 00:03:22,020
Put more snap into your wrist.

59
00:03:22,020 --> 00:03:23,420
Nah, that's not good enough.

60
00:03:23,420 --> 00:03:25,500
More rhythm, faster!

61
00:03:25,500 --> 00:03:26,980
Nyaa! Gashya! Ikugyameshuu!

62
00:03:27,220 --> 00:03:28,700
No no no no!

63
00:03:29,040 --> 00:03:29,880
Nyaa!

64
00:03:30,420 --> 00:03:33,080
Shit-gaa! Doria! Kuretebogaa!

65
00:03:33,240 --> 00:03:34,320
You idiot!

66
00:03:35,280 --> 00:03:37,100
What are you doing,
whipping all of it up like that?

67
00:03:39,800 --> 00:03:40,760
S-Man

68
00:03:40,760 --> 00:03:43,880
Fine, use the electric mixer.

69
00:03:43,880 --> 00:03:45,500
You should have let me
use that from the start!

70
00:03:46,720 --> 00:03:47,360
How's that?

71
00:03:47,720 --> 00:03:49,920
Not bad for a first try.

72
00:03:49,920 --> 00:03:52,580
Right? I also tried making this one.

73
00:03:53,160 --> 00:03:54,480
It's a Japanese-style cake.

74
00:03:55,500 --> 00:03:56,460
A Japanese-style cake?

75
00:03:56,840 --> 00:04:00,240
Yeah, I tried arranging umeboshi,
shishamo, and shumai.

76
00:04:00,640 --> 00:04:03,540
I'm spreading miso all over
it instead of whipped cream.

77
00:04:03,540 --> 00:04:08,020
And when you cut it,
there's natto sandwiched inside.

78
00:04:08,020 --> 00:04:09,160
Like anyone would buy this!

79
00:04:09,460 --> 00:04:11,460
Next, this one: curry cake.

80
00:04:12,300 --> 00:04:14,400
It's topped with real curry.

81
00:04:14,400 --> 00:04:16,120
Curry?

82
00:04:16,320 --> 00:04:18,200
There's yakisoba inside.

83
00:04:18,200 --> 00:04:21,400
You get to enjoy both curry
bread and yakisoba bread.

84
00:04:21,400 --> 00:04:22,480
No way!

85
00:04:22,480 --> 00:04:23,620
And also

86
00:04:24,720 --> 00:04:25,820
Sushi cake

87
00:04:25,820 --> 00:04:28,420
Sushi toppings on a chocolate éclair.

88
00:04:28,420 --> 00:04:30,400
Not just for Christmas or birthdays,

89
00:04:30,400 --> 00:04:32,720
cakes will sell all year round!

90
00:04:32,720 --> 00:04:34,100
No, no, no!

91
00:04:34,800 --> 00:04:36,140
Nobody's going to buy that!

92
00:04:36,540 --> 00:04:38,080
So it's no good after all?

93
00:04:38,580 --> 00:04:38,940
Well then,

94
00:04:40,120 --> 00:04:41,080
how about this one?

95
00:04:41,720 --> 00:04:43,620
That's a proper-looking cake, at least.

96
00:04:43,620 --> 00:04:44,480
At least on the outside.

97
00:04:45,420 --> 00:04:49,200
But if you stick these into
the cake one after another...

98
00:04:53,220 --> 00:04:54,640
Fireworks go up!

99
00:04:55,820 --> 00:04:59,460
Anything from this size up
to rocket fireworks is fine!

100
00:04:59,880 --> 00:05:02,220
This might actually work.

101
00:05:02,220 --> 00:05:04,660
Right? Leave the wire transfers to me.

102
00:05:05,840 --> 00:05:06,424
Well then,

103
00:05:06,474 --> 00:05:09,860
if you stick these in one
after another like this,

104
00:05:11,300 --> 00:05:11,718
Well, now,

105
00:05:11,768 --> 00:05:15,360
here's a firework cake the whole
family can enjoy at Christmas!

106
00:05:15,820 --> 00:05:16,700
I'll take that one.

107
00:05:16,700 --> 00:05:17,160
Me too.

108
00:05:17,160 --> 00:05:17,840
Here you go, one each!

109
00:05:24,100 --> 00:05:24,740
Hey

110
00:05:25,940 --> 00:05:28,440
I didn't expect it to sell this well.

111
00:05:28,780 --> 00:05:31,920
Thanks to Ryo-san,
we might get a special bonus!

112
00:05:31,920 --> 00:05:33,220
Ryo-san, Ryo-san!

113
00:05:33,220 --> 00:05:36,700
Word of the firework cake has spread,
and we've got huge orders coming in!

114
00:05:36,700 --> 00:05:41,140
They want one ten meters tall
for the garden party venue!

115
00:05:41,480 --> 00:05:44,700
See? Didn't I tell you so?

116
00:05:48,480 --> 00:05:49,620
Next, please!

117
00:05:49,620 --> 00:05:51,460
Two firework cakes, please.

118
00:05:51,460 --> 00:05:52,820
Two firework cakes, coming right up.

119
00:05:53,540 --> 00:05:55,460
Two firework cakes, got it.

120
00:05:55,460 --> 00:05:55,880
Yes.

121
00:05:55,880 --> 00:05:57,580
Please pay over here.

122
00:05:58,080 --> 00:05:58,500
Yes.

123
00:05:59,700 --> 00:06:01,500
I'll take two firework cakes too.

124
00:06:01,500 --> 00:06:02,700
It's Reiko.

125
00:06:02,700 --> 00:06:04,740
Ryo-chan, you're so popular!

126
00:06:04,740 --> 00:06:05,840
Well, it's okay.

127
00:06:05,840 --> 00:06:07,260
I heard it from the Chief.

128
00:06:07,260 --> 00:06:10,180
I hear your cake-making
skills have improved too.

129
00:06:10,180 --> 00:06:11,500
Well, yeah.

130
00:06:12,140 --> 00:06:15,780
Hey, Ryo-chan, you said before that there
was something I wanted your help with, right?

131
00:06:15,780 --> 00:06:18,380
Right. So what do you need help with?

132
00:06:18,900 --> 00:06:19,920
Making cakes.

133
00:06:20,660 --> 00:06:21,260
Cakes.

134
00:06:21,260 --> 00:06:23,380
On Christmas Eve, please.

135
00:06:23,380 --> 00:06:27,380
So that's why you got me that cake shop job.
You had this scheme in mind.

136
00:06:28,140 --> 00:06:32,080
Just as planned,
Ryo-chan mastered cake making in no time.

137
00:06:32,080 --> 00:06:35,620
Well, with my nimble hands,
it was a piece of cake.

138
00:06:35,980 --> 00:06:38,220
Right, so help me on Christmas Eve.

139
00:06:38,720 --> 00:06:41,600
Fine, but you'd better pay me well for it.

140
00:06:41,600 --> 00:06:43,740
After all, I'm a pro now.

141
00:06:44,080 --> 00:06:45,380
I know, I know.

142
00:06:49,880 --> 00:06:50,560
That husband of yours

143
00:06:53,640 --> 00:06:55,740
is at the cake shop
where he works part-time.

144
00:06:57,960 --> 00:07:00,340
A Christmas Eve date with Otohime

145
00:07:00,720 --> 00:07:01,060
Yes,

146
00:07:01,110 --> 00:07:04,760
Nana-chan pushed her serialization
schedule around to free up the day for me.

147
00:07:05,360 --> 00:07:08,220
So I have to make sure
I give her a great time.

148
00:07:08,740 --> 00:07:09,870
Where should we go?

149
00:07:09,920 --> 00:07:13,020
I suppose I should stick
with the classic spots.

150
00:07:14,000 --> 00:07:17,060
Any course that's in a magazine
like that will be packed.

151
00:07:17,060 --> 00:07:19,060
It'd be like going to watch other couples.

152
00:07:19,860 --> 00:07:20,580
I see.

153
00:07:20,580 --> 00:07:23,520
Then, is there some other unique course?

154
00:07:23,520 --> 00:07:25,240
Leave it to me.

155
00:07:25,240 --> 00:07:28,420
I'll tell you a place where you
two can get into a nice mood alone.

156
00:07:28,420 --> 00:07:29,720
Really, senpai?

157
00:07:29,720 --> 00:07:30,340
Thank you very much.

158
00:07:32,680 --> 00:07:34,580
Wow, you're pretty good at this, aren't you.

159
00:07:35,020 --> 00:07:36,340
Alright, that's finished for now.

160
00:07:36,860 --> 00:07:38,460
Going to the amusement
park on Christmas Eve...

161
00:07:38,460 --> 00:07:39,500
I see.

162
00:07:39,500 --> 00:07:42,620
She's told me every year that
I never take her anywhere, so...

163
00:07:42,620 --> 00:07:43,860
This year, for sure.

164
00:07:44,260 --> 00:07:45,580
You'd know a lot about it, Ryo-san, right?

165
00:07:47,060 --> 00:07:55,240
Will she be happy? Tell me. Let me think... Yes, I have a place in mind.
If you come with me, the admission fee is free too.

166
00:07:55,720 --> 00:08:00,840
Really? That's a big help, I'm counting on you.
Leave it to me, Ryo-san!

167
00:08:05,240 --> 00:08:10,120
Chief, please come to our company Christmas party,
and bring your grandson along!

168
00:08:10,120 --> 00:08:14,480
Well, thank you. I'd be happy to join you.

169
00:08:15,020 --> 00:08:15,740
Reiko too.

170
00:08:15,740 --> 00:08:19,180
Sorry, I can't make it on Christmas Eve.

171
00:08:19,180 --> 00:08:23,020
Now that you mention it, didn't you
say you're always busy on Christmas Eve?

172
00:08:23,500 --> 00:08:26,800
Yes, I have something I always do.
Sorry about that.

173
00:08:27,360 --> 00:08:34,140
That's too bad. This year we're preparing a
custom 10-meter-tall cake for the company garden.

174
00:08:35,040 --> 00:08:35,760
That's amazing.

175
00:08:35,760 --> 00:08:38,300
Terai, you're fine, right?

176
00:08:38,920 --> 00:08:43,580
Sorry, but I'm going to the amusement
park with my kids this Christmas Eve.

177
00:08:44,000 --> 00:08:46,380
Family time, then. It can't be helped.

178
00:08:49,140 --> 00:08:51,840
Cake shop part-time job, and helping Reiko.

179
00:08:51,840 --> 00:08:54,940
I have to get Terai's whole
family into the amusement park.

180
00:08:54,940 --> 00:08:56,980
And tonight there's Nakagawa's party?

181
00:08:56,980 --> 00:08:59,360
At this rate, I'll need more than one body.

182
00:09:01,940 --> 00:09:03,480
And then there's Honda.

183
00:09:05,040 --> 00:09:07,180
I'll just hand him that, then.

184
00:09:08,020 --> 00:09:08,420
me

185
00:09:11,960 --> 00:09:13,400
The air gets trapped -

186
00:09:13,400 --> 00:09:14,120
Aaaah!

187
00:09:14,480 --> 00:09:15,080
Good, good.

188
00:09:15,560 --> 00:09:17,080
Alright, turn it over!

189
00:09:18,800 --> 00:09:21,220
Alright,
if we just bake it right here like this,

190
00:09:21,220 --> 00:09:22,980
the sponge is done.

191
00:09:23,640 --> 00:09:24,780
It's huge.

192
00:09:24,780 --> 00:09:26,560
It's a 15-ton cake, after all.

193
00:09:27,500 --> 00:09:28,660
Alright, lift it up!

194
00:09:30,960 --> 00:09:33,760
Looks like we'll make the
evening delivery after all.

195
00:09:34,120 --> 00:09:36,660
Ryo-san, the firework setup is ready, right?

196
00:09:37,100 --> 00:09:37,940
Leave it to me.

197
00:09:37,940 --> 00:09:40,720
I'll set them up before we decorate.

198
00:09:54,100 --> 00:09:56,820
All that's left is to embed these switches,
and we're good to go.

199
00:09:59,100 --> 00:09:59,980
Done.

200
00:10:00,340 --> 00:10:03,100
If I embed them in ten spots,
one of them should hit.

201
00:10:03,680 --> 00:10:04,840
Well, time to get out.

202
00:10:04,840 --> 00:10:07,120
I need to go see Reiko after this.

203
00:10:08,980 --> 00:10:11,520
I've been going without food or
drink and pulling all-nighters.

204
00:10:11,920 --> 00:10:13,900
Right, I'm inside the cake.

205
00:10:14,120 --> 00:10:16,000
Just a little bit won't hurt.

206
00:10:16,000 --> 00:10:21,140
Delicious.

207
00:10:26,820 --> 00:10:28,900
Think I'll take a little nap.

208
00:10:31,040 --> 00:10:31,760
Alright.

209
00:10:31,760 --> 00:10:33,140
Nobody's here

210
00:10:33,860 --> 00:10:36,640
Okay!

211
00:10:36,640 --> 00:10:43,900
Okay!

212
00:10:44,120 --> 00:10:47,560
Whaaaat?!

213
00:10:47,560 --> 00:10:48,660
Whaaaat?!

214
00:10:55,460 --> 00:10:58,200
Come on, hurry up,
or we won't make it by evening!

215
00:11:03,680 --> 00:11:05,220
Right, we've got all the ingredients.

216
00:11:05,220 --> 00:11:07,380
Alright,
we've got to do our best again this year.

217
00:11:11,480 --> 00:11:13,180
So that's only twenty so far.

218
00:11:13,640 --> 00:11:14,700
It's already lunchtime.

219
00:11:14,700 --> 00:11:17,340
Ryo-chan said he'd come in the morning.

220
00:11:17,340 --> 00:11:18,920
Reiko-san?

221
00:11:18,920 --> 00:11:21,000
What are you doing?

222
00:11:21,720 --> 00:11:23,680
I'm making Christmas cakes.

223
00:11:24,140 --> 00:11:26,640
No wonder it smells so good.

224
00:11:26,640 --> 00:11:28,000
But why here?

225
00:11:28,380 --> 00:11:30,460
My apartment is being renovated.

226
00:11:30,460 --> 00:11:32,700
So I'm using this place instead.

227
00:11:32,700 --> 00:11:35,280
I have to make 200 of them by today.

228
00:11:35,900 --> 00:11:36,840
200 of them?

229
00:11:37,120 --> 00:11:38,320
Reiko, you're doing it alone?

230
00:11:38,580 --> 00:11:41,860
Yeah, Ryo-chan was supposed to help me,

231
00:11:41,860 --> 00:11:43,000
but he ditched me, didn't he?

232
00:11:43,000 --> 00:11:45,220
You shouldn't trust a guy like that.

233
00:11:45,780 --> 00:11:48,200
Hey, Reiko, your face is a little red.

234
00:11:48,200 --> 00:11:51,300
Yeah, I think I have a bit of a fever.

235
00:11:51,300 --> 00:11:54,340
Then we'll help too, right?

236
00:11:54,800 --> 00:11:57,000
Of course! Thank you.

237
00:11:57,580 --> 00:11:59,600
Reiko, what should we do?

238
00:11:59,980 --> 00:12:00,647
For now,

239
00:12:00,697 --> 00:12:04,760
let's keep finishing the Bûche de Noël
sponges as they come out of the oven.

240
00:12:06,720 --> 00:12:07,360
This one.

241
00:12:07,360 --> 00:12:08,652
A Bûche de Noël

242
00:12:08,702 --> 00:12:12,060
Didn't we decorate it and then
roll it up like a sushi roll?

243
00:12:12,060 --> 00:12:14,820
How do we even decorate this... Reiko-san!

244
00:12:15,900 --> 00:12:16,720
Reiko-san!

245
00:12:17,100 --> 00:12:17,420
Are you okay?

246
00:12:17,420 --> 00:12:17,640
Are you okay?

247
00:12:19,740 --> 00:12:21,740
She's burning up! This is bad!

248
00:12:21,840 --> 00:12:23,460
Naoko, call an ambulance right away!

249
00:12:23,620 --> 00:12:23,980
Right!

250
00:12:26,760 --> 00:12:30,180
I have to deliver the cakes...
I have to deliver the cakes...

251
00:12:30,180 --> 00:12:32,820
This is serious!
It must be a really important cake!

252
00:12:33,000 --> 00:12:35,640
But where are all 200
of them supposed to go?

253
00:12:40,700 --> 00:12:41,760
W-what is this...

254
00:12:41,760 --> 00:12:45,000
Dahlia Nursing Home: 37

255
00:12:45,000 --> 00:12:47,740
Santa Maria, private: 40

256
00:12:47,740 --> 00:12:48,540
So that means...

257
00:12:48,540 --> 00:12:49,480
Yes.

258
00:12:49,480 --> 00:12:53,520
Reiko was trying to deliver the cakes
to the places written in this memo pad.

259
00:12:53,520 --> 00:12:53,900
Right.

260
00:12:53,900 --> 00:12:56,600
What should we do about the cakes?

261
00:12:56,600 --> 00:12:58,560
We have no choice but to do it ourselves.

262
00:12:58,560 --> 00:13:01,300
Reiko's recipe should
be somewhere around here.

263
00:13:01,300 --> 00:13:03,180
We just need to look at it and make them.

264
00:13:03,180 --> 00:13:03,440
Right.

265
00:13:03,440 --> 00:13:05,220
It's Christmas Eve,
and they're all left without dates.

266
00:13:05,220 --> 00:13:07,880
Let's mobilize everyone from the traffic
division at the prefectural police.

267
00:13:07,880 --> 00:13:10,680
Reiko, don't worry about the cakes.

268
00:13:11,760 --> 00:13:12,420
We'll manage somehow.

269
00:13:15,740 --> 00:13:18,280
Now then, tonight's Christmas present

270
00:13:18,280 --> 00:13:19,440
There's still time.

271
00:13:25,220 --> 00:13:26,100
Senpai.

272
00:13:26,100 --> 00:13:28,360
It says temples are open
even on Christmas Eve.

273
00:13:28,360 --> 00:13:29,540
That's what it says here, anyway.

274
00:13:30,340 --> 00:13:32,340
Sure, they're open...

275
00:13:33,240 --> 00:13:34,360
Is this really okay?

276
00:13:35,080 --> 00:13:37,480
Honda's legs have gone numb.

277
00:13:38,260 --> 00:13:39,060
Me too.

278
00:13:39,580 --> 00:13:40,100
Senpai.

279
00:13:42,760 --> 00:13:43,680
I can't eat any more.

280
00:13:47,520 --> 00:13:48,260
Here they come!

281
00:13:56,680 --> 00:14:04,980
Hi, Bobby!

282
00:14:04,980 --> 00:14:06,100
Joe-B!

283
00:14:07,120 --> 00:14:09,060
Joe-B!

284
00:14:09,060 --> 00:14:10,040
Long time no see.

285
00:14:11,940 --> 00:14:15,440
That's a big help. Ryo-san's gone missing,
so we're short-handed.

286
00:14:15,940 --> 00:14:18,680
I brought a Marine who
works with my daughter, too.

287
00:14:19,260 --> 00:14:19,980
Thank you all.

288
00:14:22,000 --> 00:14:24,020
As expected, not everyone could come.

289
00:14:24,420 --> 00:14:26,300
You lot wait outside.

290
00:14:27,660 --> 00:14:29,160
Right, let's get started.

291
00:14:29,160 --> 00:14:31,180
Dad, slice up the good-for-nothing thinly.

292
00:14:36,200 --> 00:14:39,160
Maria-san, how is Ryo-san doing?

293
00:14:40,040 --> 00:14:41,760
Apparently it's a nasty cold.

294
00:14:41,760 --> 00:14:44,560
He broke the thermometer,
and he seems a little better, though.

295
00:14:44,560 --> 00:14:47,280
Oh no, I can't make this out.

296
00:14:47,740 --> 00:14:48,820
What's wrong?

297
00:14:48,820 --> 00:14:51,480
The fine details of Reiko's recipe...

298
00:14:51,480 --> 00:14:53,680
Even if it's written in a foreign language,
we can't read it.

299
00:14:55,120 --> 00:14:57,580
It's not English. It looks like French.

300
00:14:58,060 --> 00:15:00,400
Only the person who wrote
this would know what it means.

301
00:15:00,400 --> 00:15:02,980
But Reiko is in the hospital.

302
00:15:03,680 --> 00:15:04,040
Right!

303
00:15:05,440 --> 00:15:08,080
Then add the cocoa to the whipped cream.

304
00:15:12,040 --> 00:15:13,120
Then mix it in.

305
00:15:20,680 --> 00:15:24,520
Ryo-san's late.
You said it's free here, though.

306
00:15:24,920 --> 00:15:26,800
Papa, let's just go in already.

307
00:15:26,800 --> 00:15:28,020
Let's go in, let's go in.

308
00:15:28,020 --> 00:15:31,280
Dear, let's do that.
It's getting crowded fast.

309
00:15:37,520 --> 00:15:38,820
That's cold of you.

310
00:15:38,820 --> 00:15:39,260
Yes.

311
00:15:40,800 --> 00:15:42,960
Honda, are you all right?

312
00:15:43,780 --> 00:15:44,780
I'm fine.

313
00:15:44,780 --> 00:15:47,440
Nanako-chan,
you be careful not to catch a cold.

314
00:15:49,860 --> 00:15:53,200
Even though we're following this
guidebook's date course to the letter.

315
00:15:53,960 --> 00:15:54,760
Senpai.

316
00:16:11,300 --> 00:16:13,360
Wow, what a grand party!

317
00:16:13,780 --> 00:16:15,980
By the way, Nakagawa, have you seen Ryotsu?

318
00:16:15,980 --> 00:16:17,700
No, that's strange.

319
00:16:18,080 --> 00:16:21,800
He said he'd rush over as soon as he
finished his appointment with Reiko.

320
00:16:21,800 --> 00:16:26,280
That guy,
even though he promised Daisuke a present...

321
00:16:26,800 --> 00:16:28,280
Grandpa, it's delicious!

322
00:16:28,280 --> 00:16:29,620
I see.

323
00:16:29,620 --> 00:16:33,400
That's odd.
The senpai never passes up food, does he?

324
00:16:33,920 --> 00:16:37,600
We prepared thirty servings of roast beef for the senpai,
didn't we?

325
00:16:40,440 --> 00:16:43,280
Yes! The 200th cake is done!

326
00:16:43,280 --> 00:16:44,620
We did it.

327
00:16:45,260 --> 00:16:46,760
Reiko, is this good?

328
00:16:46,760 --> 00:16:50,140
Excellent work, everyone. Thank you all.

329
00:16:50,640 --> 00:16:52,260
All that's left is to deliver them.

330
00:16:52,260 --> 00:16:55,500
But the locations are scattered everywhere.
Will we make it in time?

331
00:16:55,500 --> 00:16:58,600
Don't worry, we'll use my unit's helicopter.

332
00:16:58,600 --> 00:17:00,060
Sorry to keep you waiting.

333
00:17:00,060 --> 00:17:02,460
And now, the climax of today!

334
00:17:02,460 --> 00:17:05,420
It's the Rocket Firework "Close Call" Cake!

335
00:17:24,980 --> 00:17:26,020
Well, everyone,

336
00:17:28,460 --> 00:17:32,420
if you stab this sword into the
cake and touch the switch inside,

337
00:17:32,420 --> 00:17:34,920
the rocket-type fireworks will launch.

338
00:17:34,920 --> 00:17:38,920
Whoever hits the target will
win this cake as a prize.

339
00:17:41,120 --> 00:17:43,220
Wow, what an amazing ship!

340
00:17:43,220 --> 00:17:46,120
This one looks much better than Ryotsu's.

341
00:17:46,120 --> 00:17:48,440
Now, the first sword cut.

342
00:17:48,440 --> 00:17:51,260
Please check your number cards.

343
00:17:51,260 --> 00:17:53,660
The first number is this one.

344
00:17:55,660 --> 00:17:57,200
It's number 214.

345
00:17:57,200 --> 00:17:58,880
Number 214.

346
00:17:59,340 --> 00:18:00,120
Missed.

347
00:18:00,120 --> 00:18:01,040
Me too.

348
00:18:01,040 --> 00:18:02,540
Too bad.

349
00:18:02,540 --> 00:18:03,320
I got it!

350
00:18:03,320 --> 00:18:04,120
Here!

351
00:18:04,920 --> 00:18:08,120
Congratulations!
Now, pick up a sword from wherever you like

352
00:18:08,120 --> 00:18:09,520
and stab it into the cake.

353
00:18:10,520 --> 00:18:12,300
I slept well.

354
00:18:13,560 --> 00:18:29,820
Uuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuuu

355
00:18:29,820 --> 00:18:31,340
Too bad. Next!

356
00:18:34,000 --> 00:18:35,160
Number 75?

357
00:18:35,160 --> 00:18:37,740
So close! It's number 175.

358
00:18:37,740 --> 00:18:39,820
Grandpa, I forgot too.

359
00:18:40,420 --> 00:18:41,820
Maybe we'll hit it next time.

360
00:18:41,820 --> 00:18:42,160
Yeah.

361
00:18:43,600 --> 00:18:44,400
W-wait, this is...

362
00:18:45,140 --> 00:18:48,100
Damn, it's already been
carried to the venue?

363
00:18:48,100 --> 00:18:51,780
Whoa! Stop! There are people in here!

364
00:18:51,780 --> 00:18:54,520
Stop it! Please, stop!

365
00:18:56,900 --> 00:19:00,160
If it comes to this,
I'll eat my way out of this cake!

366
00:19:09,820 --> 00:19:14,500
Damn it, what's the point?
Why do I have to act like an ant like this?

367
00:19:15,320 --> 00:19:18,680
This isn't the time to grumble
about being sticky all over.

368
00:19:18,680 --> 00:19:20,340
I have to get out of here fast.

369
00:19:21,340 --> 00:19:22,440
Missed again.

370
00:19:22,440 --> 00:19:24,160
Please hit the next one for sure.

371
00:19:24,160 --> 00:19:26,020
Alright, next number is...

372
00:19:30,060 --> 00:19:33,160
Since it's Christmas, we made the
helicopter look like Santa's sleigh.

373
00:19:33,160 --> 00:19:34,880
You painted it all red?

374
00:19:34,880 --> 00:19:36,180
Bobby.

375
00:19:36,760 --> 00:19:38,260
How about adding some bells too?

376
00:19:38,680 --> 00:19:40,660
It really is starting to
look like Santa's sleigh.

377
00:19:47,360 --> 00:19:49,180
Too bad, missed again.

378
00:19:50,440 --> 00:19:52,800
It's hard to hit the switch, isn't it?

379
00:19:52,800 --> 00:19:54,080
Yeah, it sure is.

380
00:19:54,080 --> 00:19:56,540
Yeah, but the senior officer
still hasn't shown up, has he?

381
00:19:57,080 --> 00:20:00,860
Honestly, he never keeps his promises.
That's just the kind of guy he is.

382
00:20:03,060 --> 00:20:04,300
W-what was that?

383
00:20:04,380 --> 00:20:05,380
What's that noise?

384
00:20:05,900 --> 00:20:08,400
What's that?

385
00:20:09,240 --> 00:20:10,600
S-Santa!

386
00:20:10,900 --> 00:20:12,620
Merry Christmas!

387
00:20:12,620 --> 00:20:14,520
Merry Christmas?

388
00:20:15,560 --> 00:20:17,760
Merry Christmas!

389
00:20:18,440 --> 00:20:19,960
Merry Christmas!

390
00:20:19,960 --> 00:20:22,420
It's not Reiko this year, is it?

391
00:20:27,480 --> 00:20:29,440
Wow, that's amazing!

392
00:20:30,180 --> 00:20:35,500
Ryo-san said we absolutely had to ride the Ferris wheel at this time.
I wonder what's up?

393
00:20:39,480 --> 00:20:41,980
Reiko-san, we've finished delivering safely.

394
00:20:42,460 --> 00:20:43,400
Thanks, everyone.

395
00:20:43,840 --> 00:20:45,880
Reiko-san, please take it easy and rest.

396
00:20:45,880 --> 00:20:49,820
Tonight, the three of us are on duty at
the station in place of Ryo and Reiko-san.

397
00:20:49,820 --> 00:20:51,960
Sorry, it's Christmas and all, but...

398
00:20:57,560 --> 00:21:00,280
The next number is 175.

399
00:21:00,280 --> 00:21:02,520
It's 175.

400
00:21:02,520 --> 00:21:04,780
Yes, we finally got one!

401
00:21:04,780 --> 00:21:05,700
Grandpa, you're amazing!

402
00:21:06,220 --> 00:21:07,320
You did it.

403
00:21:07,320 --> 00:21:10,660
Yes, number 175, congratulations!

404
00:21:10,660 --> 00:21:13,820
Now, will it hit the switch
for the rocket-shaped firework?

405
00:21:13,820 --> 00:21:17,780
If it hits,
all of these luxurious prizes will be yours.

406
00:21:17,780 --> 00:21:18,660
Go ahead.

407
00:21:20,520 --> 00:21:21,520
Here I go.

408
00:21:21,520 --> 00:21:25,180
That's right, I'm definitely going
to get that Hansen model for Daisuke.

409
00:21:30,120 --> 00:21:31,500
Nana-chan, I'm sorry.

410
00:21:31,860 --> 00:21:33,940
dragging you all over the place today.

411
00:21:34,440 --> 00:21:36,440
I'm sure none of it was any fun.

412
00:21:36,900 --> 00:21:37,430
No,

413
00:21:37,480 --> 00:21:41,980
I'm just happy I got to spend
Christmas Eve alone with Honda.

414
00:21:42,620 --> 00:21:46,480
Nana-chan, according to the
schedule the senior officer made,

415
00:21:46,900 --> 00:21:48,860
the Seibashi is the last stop.

416
00:21:49,860 --> 00:21:51,260
I wonder if something's there.

417
00:21:54,580 --> 00:21:56,100
Today was exhausting.

418
00:21:56,100 --> 00:21:57,640
But it's a pleasant kind of tired, isn't it?

419
00:21:57,640 --> 00:21:57,940
Yeah.

420
00:21:57,940 --> 00:21:59,520
Shall I make some coffee?

421
00:21:59,520 --> 00:22:00,580
Excuse me!

422
00:22:03,860 --> 00:22:07,980
That's the Santa suit I made
for Chief Ohara's grandkid.

423
00:22:07,980 --> 00:22:10,900
Damn! I didn't have to
eat anything after all!

424
00:22:11,620 --> 00:22:13,300
Hey, yes! An exit!

425
00:22:13,880 --> 00:22:16,620
Gah! It's back to the same spot!

426
00:22:16,800 --> 00:22:17,700
Damn it!

427
00:22:21,780 --> 00:22:23,480
Aaaaaah!

428
00:22:23,480 --> 00:22:24,300
Hit!

429
00:22:24,300 --> 00:22:25,240
Aaaaaah!

430
00:22:26,600 --> 00:22:28,220
Aaaaaah!

431
00:22:40,280 --> 00:22:42,500
Merry Christmas, Ryotsu!

432
00:22:42,500 --> 00:22:45,220
The senior officer made this cake, you know.

433
00:22:45,220 --> 00:22:46,020
Ryotsu did.

434
00:22:46,020 --> 00:22:47,860
Wow, how pretty.

435
00:22:47,860 --> 00:22:50,420
That caveman sure knows
how to do something stylish.

436
00:22:50,420 --> 00:22:51,000
Really.

437
00:22:51,000 --> 00:22:54,300
Wow, how pretty.

438
00:22:54,300 --> 00:22:56,700
So this is what Ryo-san was talking about.

439
00:22:56,700 --> 00:22:59,040
Good thing you wore that, dear.

440
00:22:59,040 --> 00:22:59,500
Yeah.

441
00:22:59,500 --> 00:23:01,440
Wow, Daddy, it's snowing!

442
00:23:01,440 --> 00:23:05,460
Daddy, this is my first Christmas like this!

443
00:23:08,000 --> 00:23:08,720
Beautiful.

444
00:23:08,720 --> 00:23:13,040
Senpai, I planned our outing so we'd come
here because I wanted you to see this.

445
00:23:13,040 --> 00:23:17,700
Holding hands? That's so bold of you.

446
00:23:17,700 --> 00:23:18,560
Wonderful.

447
00:23:20,040 --> 00:23:22,960
Fireworks in winter and
a white Christmas, too.

448
00:23:25,300 --> 00:23:26,780
Nana-chan.

449
00:23:26,780 --> 00:23:27,800
Okay.

450
00:23:29,320 --> 00:23:30,740
Sorry.

451
00:23:31,480 --> 00:23:32,300
Honda-san.

452
00:23:34,140 --> 00:23:35,600
Nana-chan.

453
00:23:38,980 --> 00:23:41,120
Thank you, senpai.

454
00:23:44,780 --> 00:23:46,600
Here you go, this is from Ryo-sama.

455
00:23:47,140 --> 00:23:49,980
Wow, that's two now, counting the prize.

456
00:23:56,120 --> 00:23:58,400
Why does this have to happen to me alone?

457
00:23:58,400 --> 00:24:01,220
I hate Christmas!

458
00:24:15,120 --> 00:24:20,420
An afternoon after the rain,
as if someone is calling.

459
00:24:21,760 --> 00:24:27,140
Walking while looking back,
led by the hand of Gaaja.

460
00:24:28,300 --> 00:24:34,360
That strange feeling I had back then.

461
00:24:34,360 --> 00:24:39,560
So on the arcade street's tiles,

462
00:24:39,560 --> 00:24:45,320
I tried walking only on the black ones.

463
00:24:47,840 --> 00:24:53,580
Everyone was a child once,
but everyone has forgotten.

464
00:24:54,520 --> 00:24:57,620
Politicians with their self-important faces,

465
00:24:57,620 --> 00:25:00,920
and the blue-eyeshadowed aunties too,

466
00:25:00,920 --> 00:25:06,540
try turning at that corner.

467
00:25:07,460 --> 00:25:11,760
You can meet everyone, everyone.

468
00:25:12,320 --> 00:25:19,680
Over there is Kameari
surely Kameari is there.

469
00:25:20,500 --> 00:25:24,980
Everyone, come on over to our town.

470
00:25:25,940 --> 00:25:26,500
Thank you.

